      "sequence_position": 2,
      "problem": "Is the function $f(x)={x}^{3}+8x$ even, odd, or neither?",
      "worked_solution": "Recall that\n\n- a function is even if $f(-x)=f(x)$ for all $x$\n\n- a function is odd if $f(-x)=-f(x)$ for all $x$\n\nComputing $f(-x)$ for the given function and comparing it to $f(x),$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(-x) & =(-x)^{3}+8(-x) \\\\  & =-{x}^{3}-8x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $f(-x)\\ne f(x),$ the function is not even.\n\nLastly, we compute $-f(x)$ and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-f(x) & =-({x}^{3}+8x) \\\\  & =-{x}^{3}-8x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $f(-x)=-f(x),$ the function is odd.",
